  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectCapability Include="SourceItemsFromImports" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
    Every backend is listed here, including the GPU ones, and an application excludes what it
    does not name in Application<Platform, Backend>.

    Excluding is per consuming project and does not reach this file: a .vcxitems is imported
    rather than referenced, so its items land in the importing .vcxproj and that project can
    drop one for itself - right click the file, Exclude From Build, which writes an
    ExcludedFromBuild on a ClCompile Update. Other projects sharing this file are unaffected.

    A backend that is not excluded costs its own translation unit and nothing else, because no
    framework module imports a backend module - the choice reaches FormBase as a factory rather
    than as a type. The CPU backend should never be excluded: the framework rasterizes icons
    through a CPU canvas of its own whatever the application renders with.
  -->
